 <p class="wp-block-paragraph">Hinds County voters will go to the polls Nov. 3 to select their next district attorney in a quick-turn special election to fill out the term of former District Attorney Jody Owens, who pleaded guilty over the summer to a federal bribery charge stemming from an FBI sting operation to uncover corruption in Mississippi’s capital city. </p>
 <p class="wp-block-paragraph">Mississippi Today invited candidates to answer questions about their qualifications and priorities. Their responses have been lightly edited for clarity and length. </p>
